# ── Environment reference (committed) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Documents every variable this app reads. It is NOT loaded at runtime.
# Real values live in .env.local (gitignored) for development, and in the
# hosting provider's environment settings (Vercel) for staging and production.
#
# All three are NEXT_PUBLIC_*: inlined into the bundle at BUILD time and
# frozen. Set them before a deploy builds; changing one needs a redeploy,
# not a restart. One build serves one environment.

# ── Travel backend (rahgeer-be) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read on the server (lib/content/fetchers.ts) for page content, and in the
# browser (lib/api/client.ts) for the enquiry form and the planner.
#
# REQUIRED in hosting. Unset, it falls back to http://localhost:8000 — so on
# Vercel every content fetch fails and the whole site silently renders the
# bundled fallback copy. It looks like the backend "isn't working" when it
# is only unconfigured.
#
# There is no staging backend: staging points at production too. A lead
# submitted on staging is a REAL lead in the production admin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://travel.marzitech.in

# ── Analytics (GANGADHAR, Marzi's in-house tracker) ─────────────────────────────
# Optional. BOTH default to PRODUCTION values when unset (lib/analytics/index.ts),
# so a staging deploy that leaves them blank reports its traffic as real.
# Give non-production environments their own write key if the tracker has one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRACKING_URL=https://track.marzitech.in
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRACKING_WRITE_KEY=
